2.2

Background: Provenance Semirings

Definition 2.1 (Commutative Semiring). A commutative semiring
is a tuple (𝐾, ⊕, ⊗, 0̄, 1̄) such that (𝐾, ⊕, 0̄) and (𝐾, ⊗, 1̄) are commutative monoids, ⊗ distributes over ⊕, and 0̄ ⊗ 𝑎 = 𝑎 ⊗ 0̄ = 0̄
for all 𝑎 ∈ 𝐾. A semiring is zero-divisor-free if 𝑎 ⊗ 𝑏 = 0̄ implies
𝑎 = 0̄ ∨ 𝑏 = 0̄.
Definition 2.2 (𝐾-Relation). Let 𝑈 be a finite attribute set. A 𝐾relation over 𝑈 is a function:
𝑅 : Tuples(𝑈 ) → 𝐾
with finite support, i.e., {𝑡 | 𝑅(𝑡) ≠ 0̄} is finite. When 𝐾 = B, this is
just an ordinary finite relation.

