That is, a memory model consists of a possibly empty forest
of memory trees. Each memory tree has as a top-level node,
a set of memory regions and a possibly empty sub-forest that
holds its children. Two regions in the same node are aliasing.
Children are enclosed in their parents. Siblings are separate.
