Determinizing Symbolic Execution

Consider the following x86 assembly sequence:
mov QWORD PTR [rsp-16], 1
mov DWORD PTR [rsp-24], 2
mov rax, QWORD PTR [rsp-16]
The first instruction moves the quad (8 byte) word 1 to memory location [rsp-16]. The
second moves the 4 byte word 2 to memory location [rsp-24]. The third moves 8 bytes
from memory location [rsp-16] into the RAX register. Symbolic execution should produce
the following:
s0 = sL[rsp − 16] := 1 , [rsp − 24] := 2 , RAX := 1 M
