That is, the new state s is the result of three state changes with respect to the input state s.
For sake of presentation, the instruction pointer is omitted. We illustrate that in order to
get this seemingly trivial result, we require both extra preconditions and solving of linear
equations.
Symbolic execution starts in state s and sequentially applies the presimplified semantics
of the current instruction. After execution of the first instruction, the current symbolic state
is:
