The DisassembleFunctionSignature procedure is outlined in Algorithm 2. It takes in a
function and emits the name, address, return type as well as the input names and types.
The name and address are used to maintain references to the function in lifting since it
is legal in P-Code to refer to a function by either when performing calls. Output type is
assumed to be void if it is impossible to confidently recover the function type. Figure 3.2.1
is an example comparing the source of func0 and the disassembly XML. In this example
the disassembly is fully accurate.

