3.3.1

Lift Registers and Memory References

Algorithm 5 illustrates the steps required to lift the global scope registry and memory
variables. Since register storage types in Ghidra do not necessarily include the correct
sizing nor pointer types additional analysis is required. Register values are compared
against known architecture-specific registers before lifting them to their respective types.
If neither, the register is a regular register and no additional processing is needed. Memory
locations are more straightforward and can be lifted without any additional processing.
Figure 3.3.1 shows an example of XML inputs and their resulting LLVM outputs.

