as they have pre-defined behaviours and should lift the same way each time in Ghidrall.
System functions (lines 8,21) are either pre-defined or not selected for decompilation, depending on whether or not their function is necessary for analysis. All functions are paired
with their addresses to allow indirect function calls to occur. The resulting list of functions
is then passed to the function decompilation step.

