Figure 5.1.1: A Simple Password Challenge

Figure 5.1.1 is a challenge that was created for undergraduate students. These types of
34

challenges are typically designed by security practitioners and based on real-world encounters to test and engage other engineers. When compiled, this binary takes a single
command line argument as a password and compares it against a series of checks to verify
if the password is correct. In this example, the intended password is ”reverse”.
