Other Models

NLP Models. We also tried to incorporate NLP models into
our evaluation. However, existing DL compilers still lack
complete support for basic NLP operators, such as RNN and
LSTM. Table 6 reports the results of preliminary investigation. We select two common NLP models, Char-RNN [7] and
LSTM [8], from PyTorch tutorial. Only the current version
of Glow can successfully compile both models. Thus, we
evaluated BTD with Char-RNN compiled with all versions of
Glow and LSTM compiled with Glow 2022, and BTD could
smoothly output the correct model specifications. With manual inspection, we find that typical NLP operators, such as
RNN, GRU, and LSTM, are decomposed into sub-operators
during compilation, including FC operators and Element-wise
arithmetic operators. We note that these decomposed operators are already included in the ONNX Zoo CV models [69].
Audio Processing Models. We expect that BTD can also decompile audio processing models without extension. To clarify, in the era of deep learning, audios are often converted into
2D representations and then processed using CV models [37],
or directly processed as sequences using NLP models [74].

